          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "36"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.782,
            0.104,
            0.899,
            0.121
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "MATHEMATICS"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.139,
            0.9,
            0.196
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Solution :",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Let the ten’s and the unit’s digits in the first number be x and y, respectively. "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { S o } ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , the first number may be written as "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 0 x + y"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " in the expanded form (for example, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "5 6 = 1 0 ( 5 ) + 6 )"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.203,
            0.901,
            0.261
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When the digits are reversed, x becomes the unit’s digit and y becomes the ten’s digit. This number, in the expanded notation is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 0 y   +   x"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (for example, when 56 is reversed, we get "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "6 5 = 1 0 ( 6 ) + 5 )"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.266,
            0.415,
            0.285
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "According to the given condition."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.265,
            0.291,
            0.524,
            0.309
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_12_equation_6.jpg",
          "content": "(10x + y) + (10y + x) = 66"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.315,
            0.138,
            0.332
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "i.e.,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.381,
            0.314,
            0.524,
            0.333
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_12_equation_8.jpg",
          "content": "11(x + y) = 66"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.338,
            0.138,
            0.355
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "i.e.,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.414,
            0.338,
            0.897,
            0.356
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_12_equation_10.jpg",
          "content": "x + y = 6\\tag{1}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.361,
            0.616,
            0.38
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We are also given that the digits differ by 2, therefore,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.386,
            0.159,
            0.403
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "either"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.415,
            0.386,
            0.897,
            0.404
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_12_equation_13.jpg",
          "content": "x - y = 2\\tag{2}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.412,
            0.125,
            0.425
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "or"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.415,
            0.409,
            0.897,
            0.427
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_12_equation_15.jpg",
          "content": "y - x = 2\\tag{3}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.433,
            0.86,
            0.475
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x - y = 2"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , then solving (1) and (2) by elimination, we get "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x = 4"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "y = 2"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " In this case, we get the number 42."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.102,
            0.48,
            0.872,
            0.524
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "y - x = 2"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , then solving (1) and (3) by elimination, we get "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x = 2"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "y = 4"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " In this case, we get the number 24."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.531,
            0.53,
            0.549
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, there are two such numbers 42 and 24."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.555,
            0.87,
            0.574
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Verification :",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Here "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "42+24=66"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "4 - 2 = 2"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Also "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "24 + 42 = 66"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "4 - 2 = 2"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.41,
            0.593,
            0.588,
            0.612
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "EXERCISE 3.3"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.623,
            0.899,
            0.726
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Solve the following pair of linear equations by the elimination method and the substitution method : (i) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x + y = 5"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2x - 3y = 4"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (ii) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3x + 4y = 10"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2x - 2y = 2"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (iii) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3x-5y-4=0 \\quad  and  \\quad 9x=2y+7"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (iv) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{x}{2} + \\frac{2y}{3} = -1   and   x - \\frac{y}{3} = 3"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.736,
            0.899,
            0.772
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Form the pair of linear equations in the following problems, and find their solutions (if they exist) by the elimination method :"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.17,
            0.777,
            0.898,
            0.841
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) If we add 1 to the numerator and subtract 1 from the denominator, a fraction reduces to 1. It becomes "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " if we only add 1 to the denominator. What is the fraction?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 24,
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.847,
            0.9,
            0.881
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) Five years ago, Nuri was thrice as old as Sonu. Ten years later, Nuri will be twice as old as Sonu. How old are Nuri and Sonu?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 25,
          "bbox": [
            0.435,
            0.967,
            0.563,
            0.982
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 26,
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.885,
            0.901,
            0.919
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) The sum of the digits of a two-digit number is 9. Also, nine times this number is twice the number obtained by reversing the order of the digits. Find the number."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
